use std
use amni-drive
into check_cockpit.amni
lang amni
Automated verification suite for Amni-Drive's Helium + Gold full-stack modules: `look`, `layout`, `aap`, and `gate`.
Function `main` checks every invariant and prints a concise summary line for each group, exiting with code 1 if any check fails and 0 if all pass:
1. Theme presets and WCAG contrast: iterate over every preset returned by `look::presets`. Build both its normal palette (`high_contrast` false) and its high-contrast palette (`high_contrast` true) via `look::build_palette` with custom accent 0. Verify for every preset that `look::contrast` of `ink` on `panel` is at least 7.0, `soft` on `panel` is at least 6.5, `acc` on `panel` is at least 4.5, and for the high-contrast palette `acc` on `panel` is at least 7.0. Print `ok    themes: <count> presets AAA-checked` or `FAIL` with the offending preset key.
2. Glanceable car typography: test `look::car_type_scale` across five target displays: Honda 800 by 480, Standard Car 1280 by 720, Ultrawide 1920 by 720, Portrait Car 720 by 1280, and Phone 1080 by 2400 (with user scale 1.0). Verify `telemetry_px` is at least 34.0, `button_px` is at least 16.0, `meta_px` is at least 13.5, and `min_hit_px` is at least 56.0 on every display. Print `ok    typography: 5 displays verified`.
3. All 10 cockpit layouts (0 through 9) across all 5 displays, all 3 dock modes (0 auto LHD, 1 bottom dock, 2 RHD), and both swap states (false, true): call `layout::compute_cockpit` using the display's `min_hit_px`, `gutter_px`, and `pad_px`, then call `layout::validate_cockpit`. Verify every combination (300 total layout configurations) returns 0 and has 6 buttons and at least 1 pod. Print `ok    layouts: <passed>/300 configurations valid` or `FAIL` with the first failing configuration and error code.
4. Android Auto Protocol framing and protobuf round-trip: encode a multi-frame header via `aap::encode_frame_header` (channel 3, `FLAG_FIRST`, payload 4, total 7) and decode with `aap::decode_frame_header`, verifying `header_size` is 8 and `total_length` is 7; push a 4-byte first frame and a 3-byte `FLAG_LAST` frame through `aap::reassemble_push` and verify the completed buffer has all 7 bytes in order. Also encode a varint field (field 1, value 300) and a bytes field (field 2, `"amni"`) using `aap::pb_put_tag`, `aap::pb_put_varint`, and `aap::pb_put_bytes`, then decode both with `aap::pb_next_field` and verify exact values. Print `ok    aap: framing, reassembly & protobuf verified`.
5. GPS motion classifier and driver gate: starting from a fresh `gate::MotionState`, call `gate::update_motion` at speed 0.0 and verify `STATE_PARKED`; call at 15.0 meters per second twice and verify `STATE_MOVING`; call `gate::resolve_gate` for `STATE_MOVING` with gate enabled and passenger false and verify nav (0) and media (1) return `DECISION_ALLOW` while video (3) returns `DECISION_PASSENGER_CONFIRM`. Verify `gate::haversine_meters` between (40.0, -74.0) and (40.0, -74.0) is 0.0. Print `ok    gate: motion classifier & safety policy verified`.
6. Print final line `amni-drive helium: ok` on success or `amni-drive helium: FAILED` on failure.
